WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.237
At school we speak English.

2
00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:11.648
But we speak many other languages too.

3
00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:15.159
Mrs. Berman is from Germany.

4
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.020
"Good morning, class," she says.

5
00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:25.751
"Good morning," we say in German. "Guten Morgen!"

6
00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:29.543
Koji's grandfather is from Japan.

7
00:00:29.544 --> 00:00:32.126
He visits our classroom.

8
00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:38.104
We say "welcome" in Japanese. "Yōkoso."

9
00:00:38.105 --> 00:00:40.998
Mr. Como is from Italy.

10
00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:43.908
He is our music teacher.

11
00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:49.682
We sing "hello" in Italian. "Ciao!"

12
00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:52.558
David is from China.

13
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.420
He brings dumplings from home.

14
00:00:55.421 --> 00:01:01.252
We say "thank you" in Chinese. "Xie-xie."

15
00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:04.302
Jane's friend lives in France.

16
00:01:04.303 --> 00:01:07.503
Jane teaches us words in French.

17
00:01:07.504 --> 00:01:12.362
Au revoir means "good-bye."

18
00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:15.480
Miss Isabel is from Spain.

19
00:01:15.481 --> 00:01:20.932
She makes hot soup for lunch.

20
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:27.032
"Yum!" we say in Spanish. "Es rico!"

21
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:29.938
Hana is from Korea.

22
00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:34.516
She shows us how to write in Korean.

23
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:41.456
I write "mom." "Umma."

24
00:01:41.457 --> 00:01:44.539
I can speak many languages.

25
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:50.204
What languages can you speak?

